WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Imagine someone who eats well
every day, and never once helps,

2
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.630
thanks or gives anything to anyone.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.910
One ancient Hindu scripture has a
harsh word for that person: a thief.

4
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:13.930
Not lazy.

5
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.220
Not selfish.

6
00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:19.350
A thief, as if they had
stolen from the whole world.

7
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.190
Why would taking without
giving back count as stealing?

8
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.640
In this mission, you'll read that
passage from the Bhagavad Gita,

9
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:31.450
and meet two Hindu ideas:
giving, and service to others.

10
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.730
You'll see Hindus
putting them into action,

11
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.010
then weigh up whether serving in
person is better than giving money.

12
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:43.000
Your mission: find out why taking
without giving back can count as theft.
